course: dictionary
lesson: 11783
title: Befriend: reaching out to someone
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To befriend someone means to become their friend, especially when they are new, lonely or need help. «Mia saw that Rosa was sitting alone, so she went over and befriended her.» Mia did not just say hello. She made Rosa feel welcome.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. New, lonely and needs help are the kinds of people you might befriend. «The new pupil was nervous on the first day, but Sam befriended him at lunch.» Nervous on the first day tells you the pupil was new and needed a friend.
explain: You can also befriend an animal. This means you make friends with it so it trusts you. «The fox was wary at first, but after many quiet days the farmer befriended it.» Wary at first and then trusts you show that befriending takes time and patience.
explain: Online, a stranger may pretend to be friendly so they can trick you. Be careful when someone you have never met wants to befriend you quickly. Always tell a trusted adult.
fact: Befriend means to become a friend to someone, or to make friends with an animal so that it trusts you.
fact: «Befriend» is a verb. Its forms are befriends, befriended and befriending.
fact: «Befriend a new pupil» means helping someone who is new to feel included at school.
fact: «Was befriended by» means someone became your friend: «Tom was befriended by the older boys» means they became his friends.
fact: Online, a stranger may try to befriend a child in order to trick them. If someone you do not know online wants to be your secret friend, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «The new girl sat alone, so Priya went over to befriend her.» What does befriend mean here? | To shout at her | To forget her name | *To become her friend | To run away from her
exercise: The boy befriended the shy deer, and now it comes to eat from his hand. What does befriend mean here? | *To make friends with it so it trusts you | To paint it | To count it | To chase it away
exercise: «Ella befriended the lonely man at the bus stop.» Which word is the past tense of befriend? | friendly | befriends | *befriended | befriending
test: «Sam is kind, and he likes to befriend people who feel left out.» What does befriend mean in this sentence? | To make them feel worse | *To become their friend and help them feel included | To argue with them | To ignore them
test: A stranger online writes, «Let's be secret best friends,» and tries to befriend you quickly. What should you do? | *Tell a trusted adult | Keep it a secret from everyone | Ignore it and do nothing | Send them your address
exam: Which sentence uses befriend correctly? | The bus was late again | Dad befriend the dinner in the oven | I befriend my homework every night | *Ava befriended the new girl and showed her where the library was
